1
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:03,329
Come on. Go! Go!

2
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:07,801
Michiko, you're disgraceful.
Horseracing is a noble sport.

3
00:01:09,169 --> 00:01:12,839
Oh? The Melon Seiko I bet on
is in last place.

4
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:14,574
Go, X-Homare.

5
00:01:14,841 --> 00:01:17,911
Go kick their butts!

6
00:01:24,117 --> 00:01:27,120
My horse has been
running well recently.

7
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:29,956
Legend Queen is coming from behind.

8
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:32,492
Would you run, too?

9
00:01:40,166 --> 00:01:44,270
Run desperately for me, will you?

10
00:01:46,739 --> 00:01:47,740
Yes, ma'am.

11
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:52,912
Go for it!

12
00:01:53,713 --> 00:01:55,515
Michiko, I can't see it.

13
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:58,051
Melon Seiko. Go for it!

14
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:01,721
- Go, X-Homare.
- Faster!

15
00:02:01,821 --> 00:02:05,024
That horse is in the way.

16
00:02:05,091 --> 00:02:07,794
Watch out. They're going to crash!

17
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:13,166
It's no good.
Legend Queen contacted X-Homare.

18
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:17,370
The jockey of Legend Queen fell off.
How is the race going to be?

19
00:02:17,937 --> 00:02:22,108
X-Homare, don't give up! Go for it!

20
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:26,846
Legend Queen is dragging her foot.
The jockey still can't get up...

21
00:02:26,946 --> 00:02:30,216
Is my Legend Queen all right?

22
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:37,924
Legend Queen is disqualified
due to its disturbance.

23
00:02:40,727 --> 00:02:44,030
X-Homare has finished in last place.

24
00:02:44,097 --> 00:02:45,431
Last place...

25
00:02:47,634 --> 00:02:49,836
Oh my God!

26
00:02:51,304 --> 00:02:56,075
I bet all my money on it...

27
00:02:56,876 --> 00:02:58,545
I'm sorry to hear that.

28
00:02:59,145 --> 00:03:02,115
You're not good at mahjong
or horseracing.

29
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:05,285
Your specialty is surgery only.

30
00:03:06,052 --> 00:03:09,722
Akira, I'm hungry.

31
00:03:09,789 --> 00:03:12,091
Buy me a hotdog, will you?

32
00:03:12,158 --> 00:03:14,494
Oh? Akira?

33
00:03:14,961 --> 00:03:18,164
Hey, Akira, wait up.

34
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,066
Akira!

35
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,569
I hit it. I hit the jackpot.

36
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:26,005
I hit it. I hit the jackpot.

37
00:03:26,506 --> 00:03:31,044
Where did he go? I'm starving.

38
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:39,452
Please let us through.

39
00:03:46,259 --> 00:03:47,193
I'm opening the door.

40
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:52,365
- Please help.
- Yes.

41
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:56,669
I'm Hara from Asahikawa Clinic.
Feel any pain?

42
00:03:56,803 --> 00:03:58,705
From here to here.

43
00:03:59,706 --> 00:04:00,773
How do you feel?

44
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:03,243
It's so painful.

45
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:05,778
He may have muscular defense.

46
00:04:06,212 --> 00:04:08,514
Take him to the hospital.

47
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:10,450
You shouldn't move him quickly.

48
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:15,021
MAMORU HARA
SURGERY DIVISION, ASAHIKAWA CLINIC

49
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:16,389
Michiko Daimon.

50
00:04:17,123 --> 00:04:18,758
What are you doing here?

51
00:04:23,062 --> 00:04:24,464
Remember me?

52
00:04:24,631 --> 00:04:28,301
I'm Mamoru Hara. We used to work together
at Teito Medical Hospital's 3rd Division…

53
00:04:28,368 --> 00:04:29,269
Be quiet.

54
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,272
How rude.

55
00:04:32,705 --> 00:04:35,375
You know you changed our lives.

56
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:39,312
Ignoring Busujima,
you forced Dr. Torii's surgery.

57
00:04:39,746 --> 00:04:43,483
Then Dr. Kaji and Morimoto were
sent away to the countryside.

58
00:04:44,384 --> 00:04:46,586
I'm sure
even you feel some responsibility...

59
00:04:46,653 --> 00:04:49,389
- Not one bit.
- As I expected.

60
00:04:50,890 --> 00:04:53,059
- We're ready, Dr. Hara.
- Thanks.

61
00:04:55,328 --> 00:04:57,797
- Ready? One, two...
- Wait, don't move the patient.

62
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:03,670
Oh no! He threw up blood.

63
00:05:03,836 --> 00:05:05,405
I told you.

64
00:05:05,905 --> 00:05:07,974
- His blood pressure is only 50.
- Move.

65
00:05:12,378 --> 00:05:13,579
Possible injury of spleen.

66
00:05:13,713 --> 00:05:16,783
The gastric wall is damaged.
Dose one liter of Ringer's solution.

67
00:05:16,849 --> 00:05:18,851
- Secure venous access.
- Take him gently.

68
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:21,187
Ultrasound on his abdominal cavity.

69
00:05:21,254 --> 00:05:24,223
Can be bleeding from there.
Let's move him.

70
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:25,658
One, two, three...

71
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,065
Come on, Dr. Daimon.

72
00:05:32,398 --> 00:05:35,301
Mamoru Hara.
You have a medical license.

73
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:36,502
Daimon?

74
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:39,472
- I'm starving to death.
- Hold on.

75
00:05:39,706 --> 00:05:41,341
Eating is more important?

76
00:05:41,641 --> 00:05:44,210
You're awful as a human and a doctor.

77
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:46,479
As Dr. Kaji said,

78
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:49,115
- you're a demon, not Daimon.
- Door close

79
00:05:57,056 --> 00:05:58,257
I'm starving.

80
00:06:04,230 --> 00:06:05,631
Here you go.

81
00:06:08,701 --> 00:06:13,773
Yes...

82
00:06:16,442 --> 00:06:18,077
Are you kidding me?

83
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:21,080
When a blood horse breaks its leg,

84
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:23,716
we have to put it down.

85
00:06:25,485 --> 00:06:26,753
The horse is 100 million yen.

86
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:30,556
Don't tell me to put it down so easily.

87
00:06:31,157 --> 00:06:34,327
One hundred million?
I'm sorry to hear that.

88
00:06:35,528 --> 00:06:37,463
But don't worry.

89
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:41,734
I have a doctor who can fix broken legs.

90
00:06:45,037 --> 00:06:47,874
I've never operated on a horse.

91
00:06:47,974 --> 00:06:50,676
Horses and humans are
pretty much the same.

92
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:53,346
- The size is different.
- Be quiet.

93
00:06:53,479 --> 00:06:56,516
Do the surgery
and go out for "jingisukan" BBQ.

94
00:06:56,682 --> 00:06:59,252
You can't do it.

95
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:03,456
Don't worry.
Nothing is impossible for Dr. Daimon.

96
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:07,260
Third metacarpal bone is fractured.

97
00:07:07,393 --> 00:07:10,363
Axial fracture
of the proximal sesamoid.

98
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:13,099
It's impossible. You'll fail 100%.

99
00:07:15,401 --> 00:07:16,569
What did you say?

100
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:19,872
He said you'll fail 100%.

101
00:07:20,239 --> 00:07:23,342
The horse is suffering.
We should put it down.

102
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:24,944
Let me do it.

103
00:07:25,311 --> 00:07:27,513
Weren't you listening? Why?

104
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:30,016
I don't fail.

105
00:07:45,231 --> 00:07:47,133
Shall we start?

106
00:07:49,202 --> 00:07:53,773
We conduct bolt fixation on
the third metacarpal bone.

107
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,107
We will use three bolts.

108
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:56,542
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

109
00:08:06,552 --> 00:08:07,620
- Mosquito.
- Here.

110
00:08:09,722 --> 00:08:11,190
- Suck the blood.
- Yes.

111
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,797
- Drill.
- Yes.

112
00:08:29,108 --> 00:08:30,309
- C-arm.
- Okay.

113
00:08:30,776 --> 00:08:31,644
Ready.

114
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:37,683
Switch the drill guide to 3.2mm.

115
00:08:38,818 --> 00:08:40,253
56 pin.

116
00:08:56,469 --> 00:08:57,670
She's so fast.

117
00:09:10,249 --> 00:09:12,184
Thank you.

118
00:09:14,820 --> 00:09:16,889
Don't bother other horses anymore.

119
00:09:36,542 --> 00:09:38,110
The surgery was a success?

120
00:09:38,177 --> 00:09:42,481
Yes. That doctor did a perfect job.

121
00:09:42,615 --> 00:09:45,084
I'm sorry I said you'd fail 100%.

122
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:47,753
I've never seen such excellent work.

123
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:50,990
Can I have ten packets of syrup?

124
00:09:51,123 --> 00:09:53,593
- Syrup?
- I have it ready.

125
00:09:54,126 --> 00:09:55,861
- I knew you would.
- Here.

126
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:58,531
You could've put them in the cup.

127
00:10:06,572 --> 00:10:07,506
What?

128
00:10:09,308 --> 00:10:10,843
She's not a vet.

129
00:10:12,411 --> 00:10:13,346
Are you sure?

130
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,816
You helped the jockey
who threw up blood.

131
00:10:23,689 --> 00:10:26,258
Let me explain.

132
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:31,964
Dr. Daimon is a surgeon
as well as a vet.

133
00:10:32,565 --> 00:10:36,602
Here are her veterinarian licenses
from Cuba and Japan.

134
00:10:36,836 --> 00:10:37,937
May I?

135
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:42,875
- Are they real?
- Of course.

136
00:10:42,942 --> 00:10:44,343
It doesn't matter.

137
00:10:47,413 --> 00:10:50,883
So she can operate on humans too?

138
00:10:53,085 --> 00:10:54,220
Sure.

139
00:11:19,045 --> 00:11:22,348
I can't believe it. It's a miracle.

140
00:11:22,648 --> 00:11:24,183
I can't believe it, either.

141
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:27,553
Dr. Daimon can perform surgery
on a horse too.

142
00:11:29,722 --> 00:11:31,424
That feels so good.

143
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:34,660
Dr. Daimon, won't you stay here

144
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:37,263
and treat our horses and livestock?

145
00:11:37,329 --> 00:11:39,031
It sounds fun.

146
00:11:39,231 --> 00:11:40,533
Your phone is ringing.

147
00:11:40,599 --> 00:11:41,634
Oh yeah.

148
00:11:43,135 --> 00:11:44,003
Hello?

149
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:46,439
You're still playing with the horse?

150
00:11:46,772 --> 00:11:49,308
Come back to Tokyo now.
You have a job.

151
00:11:49,608 --> 00:11:52,378
I don't know.
I just got recruited here too.

152
00:11:52,611 --> 00:11:54,346
You've been called on.

153
00:11:54,914 --> 00:11:57,516
The payment is ten million yen.

154
00:11:58,918 --> 00:12:00,953
Okay. I'll be right there.

155
00:12:01,587 --> 00:12:02,888
I should get going.

156
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,758
Asahikawa City will start to get cold.

157
00:12:06,859 --> 00:12:10,362
I'll do my best for my patients.

158
00:12:10,663 --> 00:12:12,631
You also do your best.

159
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,433
Hope I can see you somewhere...

160
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:17,036
She's not here, as I expected.

161
00:12:18,304 --> 00:12:25,277
Demon!

162
00:12:27,713 --> 00:12:30,816
<i>This is a story about</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

163
00:12:36,322 --> 00:12:39,325
<i>In 2013, the collapse</i>
<i>of Teito Medical Hospital</i>

164
00:12:39,391 --> 00:12:40,893
<i>has not stopped one bit.</i>

165
00:12:41,827 --> 00:12:45,097
I'd like to ask you all again.

166
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:48,100
Focus on cost cutbacks,

167
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:53,539
and enhance the turnover rate
of inpatients.

168
00:12:53,672 --> 00:12:58,310
That means we should put profit
before patients and our research.

169
00:12:59,478 --> 00:13:03,816
The doctors who make profit
sit at the head table,

170
00:13:03,883 --> 00:13:06,051
while we are not allowed to speak.

171
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:08,487
Doctors,

172
00:13:11,090 --> 00:13:12,825
be alarmed.

173
00:13:15,194 --> 00:13:18,364
I think that's enough.

174
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:22,802
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA, HEAD OF SURGERY
TEITO UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

175
00:13:22,868 --> 00:13:23,969
I know it's sudden,

176
00:13:24,703 --> 00:13:29,041
but we're planning to
have the chairperson election.

177
00:13:31,844 --> 00:13:33,412
- Sir.
- Yes?

178
00:13:33,779 --> 00:13:36,115
We had the election six months ago.

179
00:13:36,248 --> 00:13:38,851
We have finally settled down.

180
00:13:39,251 --> 00:13:41,554
Another election will confuse our staff.

181
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:42,721
So?

182
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:48,194
When I say do it, do it.

183
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:51,897
I'm sorry.

184
00:13:54,967 --> 00:14:00,139
Takano, you seem to
be working too much.

185
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:05,377
Why don't you go back to
your hometown, Kanazawa?

186
00:14:06,111 --> 00:14:08,414
I already received paid vacations.

187
00:14:08,547 --> 00:14:09,648
I don't mean a vacation.

188
00:14:12,484 --> 00:14:13,419
This is a transfer.

189
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:17,389
Chairperson Takano, as of today,

190
00:14:17,723 --> 00:14:23,429
you are transferred to
the 18th branch in Kanazawa.

191
00:14:25,097 --> 00:14:26,599
Why?

192
00:14:27,132 --> 00:14:31,837
I've worked hard to increase
the number of inpatients and operations.

193
00:14:32,238 --> 00:14:34,173
Now I relocate?

194
00:14:34,573 --> 00:14:37,109
The chairperson position
in the 2nd surgery dept. is vacant.

195
00:14:38,010 --> 00:14:39,645
We will have an election.

196
00:14:40,179 --> 00:14:43,349
If you'd like to run,
or to nominate someone,

197
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:46,151
report it to the election committee.

198
00:14:46,485 --> 00:14:48,787
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

199
00:14:49,255 --> 00:14:51,523
<i>The medical office of the university</i>
<i>has weakened,</i>

200
00:14:51,824 --> 00:14:54,126
<i>and the hierarchy of doctors</i>
<i>has collapsed.</i>

201
00:14:54,193 --> 00:14:58,397
Yes, sir!

202
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:01,634
That's it.

203
00:15:03,435 --> 00:15:04,603
We're done.

204
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:12,244
<i>The medical world has become a place</i>
<i>where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

205
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,714
<i>Being a surgeon used to be</i>
<i>a glamorous job,</i>

206
00:15:16,215 --> 00:15:19,018
<i>but now there are fewer candidates</i>
<i>due to harsh conditions.</i>

207
00:15:19,652 --> 00:15:22,454
<i>Many doctors have left the medical field.</i>

208
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:25,958
Your time has come, Prof. Ebina.

209
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:28,794
Elections are unpredictable.

210
00:15:29,061 --> 00:15:32,331
- There's no one but you.
- Exactly.

211
00:15:44,677 --> 00:15:45,811
Greetings, sir.

212
00:15:46,078 --> 00:15:47,579
Greetings, sir.

213
00:15:48,547 --> 00:15:49,515
Make your rounds.

214
00:15:57,389 --> 00:16:00,459
<i>Executive Manager</i>
<i>of the surgery dept., Dr. Hiruma,</i>

215
00:16:00,993 --> 00:16:04,096
<i>makes his rounds</i>
<i>for the 2nd surgery department.</i>

216
00:16:06,365 --> 00:16:08,600
<i>To cover the critical situation,</i>

217
00:16:08,701 --> 00:16:11,804
<i>a new type of doctor has emerged.</i>

218
00:16:12,504 --> 00:16:16,709
<i>Generally, doctors work in hospitals</i>
<i>or have their own clinic.</i>

219
00:16:17,609 --> 00:16:22,047
<i>The authority of medical office</i>
<i>controls doctors in a hospital.</i>

220
00:16:22,681 --> 00:16:25,250
<i>However, freelance physicians</i>

221
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:29,955
<i>who don't belong to university</i>
<i>medical offices have appeared.</i>

222
00:16:31,357 --> 00:16:33,559
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

223
00:16:34,893 --> 00:16:38,664
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

224
00:16:39,765 --> 00:16:44,636
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

225
00:17:08,394 --> 00:17:10,429
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>
<i>also known as…</i>

226
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:14,166
<i>"Doctor-X."</i>

227
00:17:47,099 --> 00:17:49,601
- Good morning.
- Good morning, sir.

228
00:17:53,305 --> 00:17:55,941
SURGERY DEPARTMENT CONFERENCE

229
00:17:56,008 --> 00:17:57,176
Shall we begin?

230
00:17:58,343 --> 00:18:02,247
The executive manager
of internal medicine

231
00:18:02,314 --> 00:18:03,882
will join us as a special guest today.

232
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:06,518
The operation scheduled on the 3rd

233
00:18:07,186 --> 00:18:10,022
is a special patient introduced by her.

234
00:18:10,155 --> 00:18:11,790
Please explain, Prof. Mabuchi.

235
00:18:14,159 --> 00:18:17,596
I'm Mabuchi from
the internal medicine department.

236
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:24,236
Oh my!

237
00:18:25,671 --> 00:18:27,506
Looks like an army.

238
00:18:27,573 --> 00:18:29,675
SHINOBU KONDO
2ND SURGERY DEPARTMENT

239
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:32,077
They are doing great, aren't they?

240
00:18:32,678 --> 00:18:37,749
As you said, I've trained them
very strictly like an army.

241
00:18:37,883 --> 00:18:41,820
It's a waste of time.
Please sit down.

242
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:46,458
Sit down.

243
00:18:52,164 --> 00:18:54,700
Let's get to the point.

244
00:18:55,701 --> 00:18:59,705
The patient is 58, female.

245
00:19:00,172 --> 00:19:02,808
I can't tell her name.

246
00:19:02,941 --> 00:19:06,378
She strongly wishes to
be hospitalized in privacy.

247
00:19:06,512 --> 00:19:08,947
- A patient with secret reasons.
- A politician?

248
00:19:09,014 --> 00:19:10,449
Could be a celebrity.

249
00:19:10,582 --> 00:19:14,386
Having no name is inconvenient.

250
00:19:14,453 --> 00:19:15,521
Right.

251
00:19:17,189 --> 00:19:19,224
Excuse me, Dr. Mabuchi.

252
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:22,661
During the special patient's
hospitalization...

253
00:19:22,761 --> 00:19:26,365
Could we call her by a fake name
like Junko Yamaguchi?

254
00:19:27,299 --> 00:19:31,303
Can we call her that?

255
00:19:31,436 --> 00:19:37,676
Sure. These are the test results
of Junko Yamaguchi from a week ago.

256
00:19:38,076 --> 00:19:43,115
On her left femur's distal portion,
extraskeletal chondrosarcoma

257
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,017
is from the front side to the back.

258
00:19:45,150 --> 00:19:49,321
The tumor size is 8 cm.
Early operation is required.

259
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:54,626
- And the surgeon is...
- Hold on.

260
00:19:55,327 --> 00:19:58,931
This is the surgical
department conference.

261
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:02,634
As Executive Manager,
I host the meeting from here.

262
00:20:02,768 --> 00:20:05,037
- But this patient...
- Prof. Ebina.

263
00:20:05,404 --> 00:20:08,707
- Yes.
- How will you diagnose the patient?

264
00:20:08,941 --> 00:20:12,678
For this progression, preservation
of the limb is impossible.

265
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:16,014
Femur amputation is the only choice.

266
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:17,749
I agree.

267
00:20:19,017 --> 00:20:24,423
Then we will ask Mizuno from orthopedic
to perform surgery.

268
00:20:25,324 --> 00:20:26,291
I understand.

269
00:20:27,326 --> 00:20:28,327
Objection.

270
00:20:40,272 --> 00:20:41,573
Who the heck is she?

271
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:44,343
Is she a hostess to collect the bill?

272
00:20:44,943 --> 00:20:46,111
Why is she at the conference?

273
00:20:50,782 --> 00:20:52,718
Is she...Hiruma's lover?

274
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:56,488
- No way.
- Hey, you. Miss.

275
00:20:57,189 --> 00:20:59,625
Who are you?

276
00:21:00,092 --> 00:21:02,060
Answer him.

277
00:21:02,327 --> 00:21:05,764
How dare you sneak into
the sacred conference room?

278
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:07,733
I still object.

279
00:21:09,534 --> 00:21:13,572
- I would perform the AO treatment.
- What?

280
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:16,808
She'll be unable to walk
if her femur is amputated.

281
00:21:17,142 --> 00:21:20,879
While preserving bone and vessel,
remove the tumor.

282
00:21:21,179 --> 00:21:24,416
Then inject the AO solutions
and beam on it.

283
00:21:24,716 --> 00:21:28,487
This is how to remove
any debris of tumor cells.

284
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:31,890
For the patient's sake,
amputation is impossible.

285
00:21:32,724 --> 00:21:34,793
It has to be the AO treatment.

286
00:21:35,093 --> 00:21:39,064
Okay. I heard your opinion.

287
00:21:40,399 --> 00:21:45,504
Before that, answer my question.

288
00:21:48,407 --> 00:21:49,541
Who do you think you are?

289
00:21:50,876 --> 00:21:54,346
Kanbara Doctor Agency sent me here.
I'm Michiko Daimon.

290
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:55,747
Doctor Agency?

291
00:21:55,847 --> 00:21:57,749
Michiko Daimon?

292
00:21:58,016 --> 00:22:01,453
I'm terribly sorry.
I'll throw her out now.

293
00:22:01,620 --> 00:22:06,191
A prestigious hospital like ours
would hire someone like you?

294
00:22:06,558 --> 00:22:07,726
Get out now.

295
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:09,761
I was called to come here.

296
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,731
- By whom?
- I don't know the client.

297
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:15,100
I was told to come here at 9:00.

298
00:22:15,233 --> 00:22:16,401
Stop the nonsense.

299
00:22:16,535 --> 00:22:19,938
- I'm very sorry.
- We'll get rid of her now.

300
00:22:21,373 --> 00:22:22,708
Stop it.

301
00:22:25,477 --> 00:22:27,279
I called her.

302
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:29,381
What? You did?

303
00:22:30,816 --> 00:22:33,185
You should've said so earlier.

304
00:22:36,788 --> 00:22:40,292
You wore the white fur coat
in Hokkaido.

305
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:42,794
- The horse owner!
- What are you talking about?

306
00:22:42,928 --> 00:22:44,796
Executive Director Mabuchi,

307
00:22:46,598 --> 00:22:48,433
what is this all about?

308
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:54,172
I called her to perform surgery
on my patient.

309
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:05,650
How could the operation
of Teito Medical University Hospital

310
00:23:06,618 --> 00:23:12,791
be performed
by some unknown freelancer?

311
00:23:13,024 --> 00:23:14,593
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

312
00:23:16,928 --> 00:23:19,064
There's another "Yes Sir Brothers."

313
00:23:19,297 --> 00:23:21,466
What did you say?

314
00:23:21,933 --> 00:23:23,135
Please calm down.

315
00:23:23,702 --> 00:23:27,005
Dr. Daimon is a talented surgeon

316
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:30,842
who worked at our third branch
up until last year.

317
00:23:31,176 --> 00:23:37,048
My patient strongly wishes to
be cured without after-effects.

318
00:23:37,215 --> 00:23:40,919
She chose Dr. Daimon…

319
00:23:41,686 --> 00:23:43,288
as her surgeon.

320
00:23:45,023 --> 00:23:48,994
Prof. Hiruma, do you have
anything else to say?

321
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:55,867
No.

322
00:23:58,336 --> 00:24:02,107
We have no choice.
This is the patient's request.

323
00:24:03,008 --> 00:24:04,109
I understand.

324
00:24:06,311 --> 00:24:09,181
Michiko Daimon?

325
00:24:10,682 --> 00:24:11,817
For this time only,

326
00:24:13,185 --> 00:24:17,355
you're allowed to perform the surgery

327
00:24:18,990 --> 00:24:21,059
as a special medical staff.

328
00:24:22,194 --> 00:24:23,228
Prof. Ebina,

329
00:24:24,095 --> 00:24:28,700
please take care of her
in the 2nd surgery department.

330
00:24:30,535 --> 00:24:31,470
Yes, sir.

331
00:24:31,536 --> 00:24:35,407
However, you must follow
the hospital's rules.

332
00:24:37,108 --> 00:24:42,614
First, do not walk around
this facility in your lingerie.

333
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:47,085
These are my regular clothes.

334
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:48,253
Do not talk back.

335
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:52,390
If you're a doctor,
wear appropriate clothes.

336
00:24:52,524 --> 00:24:55,227
It's irrelevant to a medical license.

337
00:24:55,527 --> 00:24:57,496
- So what?
- Compare with these things…

338
00:24:57,629 --> 00:24:58,964
Those images are too unclear.

339
00:24:59,030 --> 00:25:02,067
The vessels, nerves, and tumor
can't be easily distinguished.

340
00:25:02,901 --> 00:25:05,103
A perfect operation is impossible.

341
00:25:06,404 --> 00:25:09,307
This one and this.

342
00:25:10,308 --> 00:25:11,510
Redo the test.

343
00:25:11,810 --> 00:25:13,211
Who do you think you're ordering?

344
00:25:13,712 --> 00:25:15,514
The oldest one
of the "Yes Sir Brothers."

345
00:25:16,481 --> 00:25:17,315
That's enough!

346
00:25:17,649 --> 00:25:19,150
- You're scary.
- What?

347
00:25:21,553 --> 00:25:22,654
Your face is scary.

348
00:25:30,662 --> 00:25:32,264
Is my face that scary?

349
00:25:33,565 --> 00:25:36,368
Why do we have to accept her?

350
00:25:36,434 --> 00:25:39,471
It's a crucial time
to prepare for the election.

351
00:25:39,538 --> 00:25:42,440
She'll be gone soon.
Let's assume she doesn't exist.

352
00:25:42,574 --> 00:25:44,709
I see. Let's ignore her.

353
00:25:45,677 --> 00:25:48,413
- Hey, watch out.
- Are you hurt?

354
00:25:49,414 --> 00:25:51,383
Where is the medical office?

355
00:25:57,656 --> 00:25:59,658
Dr. Daimon, this way.

356
00:26:03,328 --> 00:26:06,131
I'm Kondo from the 2nd surgery department.
Follow me.

357
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:13,038
MEDICAL OFFICE
2ND SURGERY DEPARTMENT

358
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:21,112
Where is my desk?

359
00:26:28,787 --> 00:26:30,622
Well, I'll use this one.

360
00:26:39,664 --> 00:26:40,732
I'll use this one.

361
00:26:48,373 --> 00:26:49,674
PLEASE ENTER PASSWORD

362
00:26:50,475 --> 00:26:52,844
Tell me the password.

363
00:26:53,878 --> 00:26:55,113
What is the password?

364
00:26:55,180 --> 00:26:56,681
SHU AYUKAWA
2ND SURGERY DEPARTMENT

365
00:26:58,450 --> 00:26:59,651
Am I being ignored?

366
00:27:06,157 --> 00:27:07,626
I don't mind,

367
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:12,197
but I can't do the operation
without the medical chart.

368
00:27:13,164 --> 00:27:14,399
Hey.

369
00:27:18,370 --> 00:27:20,505
Please use mine.

370
00:27:24,709 --> 00:27:25,610
Here.

371
00:27:26,177 --> 00:27:27,012
Thanks.

372
00:27:36,154 --> 00:27:38,256
JUNKO YAMAGUCHI
(PSEUDONYM)

373
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:44,195
TEMPORARY EMPLOYEE CARD

374
00:27:50,201 --> 00:27:51,369
Here.

375
00:27:52,437 --> 00:27:53,571
Are you a freelancer too?

376
00:27:54,105 --> 00:27:56,841
No. But I can't get used to that office.

377
00:27:58,943 --> 00:28:03,214
You were with
Executive Manager Mabuchi in Hokkaido.

378
00:28:03,281 --> 00:28:05,050
We had a conference in Hokkaido.

379
00:28:06,217 --> 00:28:11,656
Conference? You guys looked like
a companion and his patron.

380
00:28:14,993 --> 00:28:16,928
I'll pay for this.

381
00:28:17,862 --> 00:28:19,964
You can keep me quiet with that?

382
00:28:20,065 --> 00:28:23,034
It's not like that.
I want to do the operation.

383
00:28:24,169 --> 00:28:28,139
As the seniority rule,
I can only perform simple surgery.

384
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:29,774
I'm so frustrated.

385
00:28:31,376 --> 00:28:34,212
Can you let me do that operation?

386
00:28:34,679 --> 00:28:35,580
No way.

387
00:28:36,281 --> 00:28:40,118
If I pass up this 10 million job,
my manager would kill me.

388
00:28:42,287 --> 00:28:43,188
It was delicious.

389
00:28:44,689 --> 00:28:46,858
Can I be your assistant then?

390
00:28:48,093 --> 00:28:49,327
Please.

391
00:28:51,796 --> 00:28:53,264
Michiko Daimon.

392
00:28:53,932 --> 00:28:57,302
From Totei University
Medical School,

393
00:28:57,736 --> 00:29:00,338
she transferred to
Cubanacan Medical School in Cuba.

394
00:29:00,638 --> 00:29:01,806
Practiced in remote areas,

395
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:05,176
a military physician,
a ship's surgeon, and a vet?

396
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:11,149
Specialty: surgery?
Hobby: surgery?

397
00:29:11,382 --> 00:29:13,685
What a joke.

398
00:29:14,319 --> 00:29:15,253
Excuse me.

399
00:29:16,187 --> 00:29:19,124
No tumors are detected
on vessels or nerves.

400
00:29:19,190 --> 00:29:22,660
The tumor has been
getting closer to the femur.

401
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:27,532
Only one week has passed
since the last test.

402
00:29:27,832 --> 00:29:30,268
May I see the patient
before surgery?

403
00:29:31,369 --> 00:29:32,771
No, you may not.

404
00:29:33,071 --> 00:29:35,840
She will be here on the surgery date.

405
00:29:36,074 --> 00:29:40,545
I'll give you all her data,
and I'll get her to sign the consent.

406
00:29:40,678 --> 00:29:42,380
You don't need to see her.

407
00:29:42,847 --> 00:29:46,384
- Seeing her in person will help...
- As executive manager,

408
00:29:46,985 --> 00:29:49,921
I will take full responsibility.

409
00:29:50,021 --> 00:29:51,990
Let me see the patient directly.

410
00:29:53,424 --> 00:29:56,294
I've never conducted surgery
without doing that.

411
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:00,665
When I say no, that means no.

412
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:04,102
Based on my diagnosis,

413
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:08,306
you just perform the surgery
based on what I tell you.

414
00:30:09,541 --> 00:30:13,244
I am not your horse.

415
00:30:26,124 --> 00:30:27,192
Excuse me.

416
00:30:27,892 --> 00:30:28,726
How can we help you?

417
00:30:29,394 --> 00:30:31,963
A professor of this hospital
is going to easily

418
00:30:33,164 --> 00:30:38,203
let some part-time surgeon
take over the operation?

419
00:30:38,269 --> 00:30:41,039
- But...
- The chairperson election is soon.

420
00:30:41,973 --> 00:30:46,244
You must perform surgery
for the special patient.

421
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:49,514
At the conference,

422
00:30:50,782 --> 00:30:53,952
I let Executive Manager Mabuchi
look good.

423
00:30:54,485 --> 00:30:56,120
But she's shrewd.

424
00:30:58,022 --> 00:30:59,591
To make herself look good,

425
00:30:59,657 --> 00:31:03,094
I know she'll report
to the board committee

426
00:31:03,394 --> 00:31:04,796
while adding false information.

427
00:31:05,630 --> 00:31:07,365
"Our surgery department is not good,

428
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:13,204
so I brought the talented surgeon

429
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:16,741
for our special patient."

430
00:31:18,576 --> 00:31:21,112
She would definitely say that.

431
00:31:21,479 --> 00:31:22,881
Yes, sir.

432
00:31:23,014 --> 00:31:25,550
Prof. Mizuno will perform the surgery.

433
00:31:25,850 --> 00:31:26,684
Leave it to me.

434
00:31:26,918 --> 00:31:29,287
I will be his first assistant.

435
00:31:29,354 --> 00:31:32,724
- I'll be the second.
- I'll be the third.

436
00:31:33,224 --> 00:31:37,028
Don't let the internal medicine
department do what they want.

437
00:31:38,263 --> 00:31:43,268
The operating room is a holy place
for us surgeons.

438
00:31:43,568 --> 00:31:44,802
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

439
00:31:45,703 --> 00:31:47,605
- You're late.
- I'm still not used to it.

440
00:31:47,939 --> 00:31:49,340
Not used to it?

441
00:31:49,474 --> 00:31:51,342
- You always watch them, don't you?
- Yes, sir.

442
00:32:06,691 --> 00:32:08,993
It's time for me to leave. Goodbye.

443
00:32:35,820 --> 00:32:38,122
Something wrong, Dr. Daimon?

444
00:32:41,125 --> 00:32:43,261
You always wear high heels?

445
00:32:45,563 --> 00:32:47,899
I don't wear heels less than 10cm.

446
00:32:50,168 --> 00:32:51,169
I see.

447
00:32:51,436 --> 00:32:53,404
Thanks for your hard work.

448
00:32:54,272 --> 00:32:56,474
Don't wear manicure for the surgery.

449
00:33:00,445 --> 00:33:02,513
Tell that to your patient.

450
00:33:10,521 --> 00:33:12,123
You went to Hokkaido?

451
00:33:12,256 --> 00:33:15,994
You also went on a cruise
as a ship's doctor. For a training?

452
00:33:16,627 --> 00:33:20,298
You should polish
your feminine skills more.

453
00:33:20,365 --> 00:33:22,000
Thanks for waiting.

454
00:33:22,166 --> 00:33:25,603
What's this?
It's a brand new mahjong table!

455
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:27,872
While you were out, I bought a new one.

456
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:30,808
- Here.
- Push the button?

457
00:33:39,450 --> 00:33:40,785
How is the main branch?

458
00:33:41,119 --> 00:33:45,456
All the doctors look down on people,
and they are so nasty.

459
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:47,859
They are slaves of professors.

460
00:33:47,992 --> 00:33:51,429
They take out their frustration on you.

461
00:33:51,562 --> 00:33:53,564
Hospitals are all alike.

462
00:33:53,631 --> 00:33:57,802
I was surprised the horse owner
is the boss of internal medicine.

463
00:33:57,935 --> 00:33:59,937
Internal medicine's executive manager?

464
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:02,607
a.k.a. the queen of Teito Hospital.

465
00:34:02,774 --> 00:34:04,809
- What is it?
- I have something to report.

466
00:34:05,276 --> 00:34:08,112
Ebina and the others
are planning something.

467
00:34:08,813 --> 00:34:12,517
Stop it.
This operation must be done by Daimon.

468
00:34:12,850 --> 00:34:16,087
It has to be her? What do you mean?

469
00:34:16,154 --> 00:34:20,024
You don't need to be interested in her.

470
00:34:21,292 --> 00:34:24,529
<i>Kazuyo Mabuchi has used everything</i>

471
00:34:24,595 --> 00:34:27,465
<i>to climb up to her current position.</i>

472
00:34:28,032 --> 00:34:29,634
There are rumors that...

473
00:34:30,435 --> 00:34:34,205
she was Prof. Hiruma's first lover.

474
00:34:34,272 --> 00:34:38,843
No way! That Hiruma?
The fat guy with the mustache?

475
00:34:39,377 --> 00:34:42,947
<i>He has many lovers</i>
<i>inside and outside the hospital.</i>

476
00:34:45,950 --> 00:34:47,685
- How are you?
- You're working hard.

477
00:34:48,252 --> 00:34:49,454
Lisa.

478
00:34:50,421 --> 00:34:54,692
Why don't you believe in
your patients' natural healing power

479
00:34:55,126 --> 00:34:56,360
and go out with me tonight?

480
00:34:56,461 --> 00:34:59,597
I'm sorry. I have a night shift.

481
00:34:59,797 --> 00:35:01,566
That's too bad.

482
00:35:05,369 --> 00:35:08,506
How about you?
I know a good pork restaurant.

483
00:35:09,173 --> 00:35:10,208
Prof. Hiruma.

484
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:13,244
Okay. Let's go. Have a good evening.

485
00:35:13,444 --> 00:35:15,413
It's all right.

486
00:35:15,580 --> 00:35:19,484
<i>He got promoted quickly,</i>
<i>and he's quick with women too.</i>

487
00:35:20,485 --> 00:35:25,623
Now Kazuyo Mabuchi
is getting in Hiruma's way.

488
00:35:25,756 --> 00:35:26,924
Getting in his way?

489
00:35:26,991 --> 00:35:32,096
She's considered to be the best bet
for the next hospital director.

490
00:35:33,498 --> 00:35:37,335
Women who have obtained power
can be so greedy.

491
00:35:37,401 --> 00:35:39,904
Who is the patient you'll operate?

492
00:35:40,171 --> 00:35:42,406
She must be a big shot because

493
00:35:42,707 --> 00:35:45,076
her face and name are secrets.

494
00:35:45,543 --> 00:35:49,280
It can be a person
from the imperial family.

495
00:35:49,747 --> 00:35:53,584
If so, ten million is too cheap.
I should've asked for more.

496
00:35:53,951 --> 00:35:58,189
Do I still have a lot of debt left, Akira?

497
00:35:58,456 --> 00:36:00,091
You do.

498
00:36:01,058 --> 00:36:05,062
How much was this mahjong table?

499
00:36:05,763 --> 00:36:07,431
I got some extra payment.

500
00:36:07,732 --> 00:36:11,669
Didn't it come from my operation?

501
00:36:11,903 --> 00:36:14,906
Michiko. Ron.

502
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:19,443
Full Outside, Three Color Straight,
Double Run, and two Doras.

503
00:36:19,510 --> 00:36:20,545
That's a Baiman!

504
00:36:22,079 --> 00:36:24,348
It's not fair!

505
00:36:38,296 --> 00:36:40,498
Good luck on today's surgery.

506
00:36:40,565 --> 00:36:42,600
- Is everyone inside?
- Nobody is here.

507
00:36:44,535 --> 00:36:46,204
- It's just you?
- I am sorry.

508
00:36:46,537 --> 00:36:48,439
All of the staff rejected this surgery.

509
00:36:48,973 --> 00:36:52,143
- You need more than one assistant?
- Of course.

510
00:36:54,145 --> 00:36:56,080
Do the work of five assistants.

511
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:03,054
- Prof. Ebina.
- We have a lot of assistants.

512
00:37:03,120 --> 00:37:05,223
Mizuno will perform this surgery.

513
00:37:06,190 --> 00:37:08,359
- Why?
- The patient's condition has changed.

514
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:12,763
It's urgent. Prof. Hiruma decided
he can't leave it to you.

515
00:37:12,897 --> 00:37:15,700
- I didn't hear it.
- Prof. Mizuno, please.

516
00:37:26,777 --> 00:37:28,312
When is the patient coming?

517
00:37:29,447 --> 00:37:31,682
She's doing premedication.

518
00:37:37,388 --> 00:37:38,356
What do you want?

519
00:37:40,491 --> 00:37:42,226
- Get out.
- You get out.

520
00:37:42,293 --> 00:37:44,528
- Which one will perform?
- Me.

521
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:46,264
Please figure it out.

522
00:37:46,497 --> 00:37:49,066
- I haven't seen that anesthetist.
- Who are you?

523
00:37:49,734 --> 00:37:52,003
I was hired along with Dr. Daimon.

524
00:37:52,069 --> 00:37:54,105
Jonouchi from Kanbara Doctor Agency.

525
00:37:54,505 --> 00:37:56,140
It's been a while.

526
00:37:56,774 --> 00:37:59,110
Geez. Another freelancer.

527
00:38:02,179 --> 00:38:04,282
- The surgery starts soon.
- Okay.

528
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:13,124
Dr. Daimon.

529
00:38:13,924 --> 00:38:14,759
Daimon?

530
00:38:16,027 --> 00:38:19,530
You're not the surgeon here anymore.

531
00:38:20,431 --> 00:38:22,667
Leave this room.

532
00:38:23,601 --> 00:38:25,369
Leave it to Prof. Mizuno.

533
00:38:26,504 --> 00:38:29,974
Look at those eyes of her.

534
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:32,510
How scary.

535
00:38:34,011 --> 00:38:36,380
I conduct the operation. Move.

536
00:38:36,447 --> 00:38:37,381
It's my patient.

537
00:38:37,515 --> 00:38:39,150
You're just a part-timer.

538
00:38:39,250 --> 00:38:40,618
I'll raise your rate, so go home.

539
00:38:40,751 --> 00:38:44,055
You need part-timers' help
to perform the surgery, right?

540
00:38:44,455 --> 00:38:45,356
What did you say?

541
00:38:51,128 --> 00:38:53,331
Junko Yamaguchi is coming in.

542
00:39:06,077 --> 00:39:06,944
Prof. Mabuchi...

543
00:39:07,945 --> 00:39:09,380
I knew it.

544
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:12,983
No way.

545
00:39:13,050 --> 00:39:14,685
What a surprise.

546
00:39:15,086 --> 00:39:17,254
Prof. Mabuchi is the patient.

547
00:39:17,388 --> 00:39:20,624
This is something.

548
00:39:21,926 --> 00:39:23,561
I'll report it to the director.

549
00:39:30,468 --> 00:39:32,470
Oh my goodness.

550
00:39:34,105 --> 00:39:38,943
You even kept it a secret
from me, Kazuyo?

551
00:39:44,782 --> 00:39:46,317
OPERATION CONSENT FORM

552
00:39:46,450 --> 00:39:47,852
SIGNED: KAZUYO MABUCHI

553
00:39:54,525 --> 00:39:55,626
Let's start.

554
00:39:55,926 --> 00:39:58,396
- Daimon.
- Answer me, Daimon!

555
00:39:58,562 --> 00:39:59,397
Scalpel.

556
00:39:59,997 --> 00:40:01,098
Hold on.

557
00:40:02,833 --> 00:40:08,873
Now we know our executive manager
of internal medicine is the patient.

558
00:40:09,573 --> 00:40:13,544
Michiko Daimon,
do not touch the patient.

559
00:40:13,711 --> 00:40:16,080
The patient asked me to do this.

560
00:40:16,213 --> 00:40:17,915
You can't follow his order?

561
00:40:19,316 --> 00:40:20,951
- Don't touch me.
- Get out.

562
00:40:22,453 --> 00:40:27,057
Prof. Mizuno
conducts the femur amputation.

563
00:40:27,291 --> 00:40:28,793
Go on, Prof. Mizuno.

564
00:40:29,059 --> 00:40:30,428
- Scalpel.
- Wait.

565
00:40:30,895 --> 00:40:32,663
She doesn't want the amputation.

566
00:40:34,098 --> 00:40:35,599
You'll make her unable to walk?

567
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:46,777
My patient strongly wishes to
be cured without after-effects.

568
00:40:51,048 --> 00:40:56,086
The AO treatment could save
the patient's nerves and vessels,

569
00:40:56,587 --> 00:40:58,956
but the tumors infiltrate the femur.

570
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:01,859
Full recovery is unsure,
and recurrence can be possible.

571
00:41:02,626 --> 00:41:04,094
I agree.

572
00:41:05,763 --> 00:41:09,266
Prof. Mizuno, go on.

573
00:41:14,138 --> 00:41:15,773
I'll change the operative method.

574
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:17,975
Bring liquid nitrogen. Hurry.

575
00:41:18,409 --> 00:41:20,377
- Liquid nitrogen?
- What for?

576
00:41:20,544 --> 00:41:22,046
Change the method?

577
00:41:22,112 --> 00:41:23,681
I have her permission.

578
00:41:25,115 --> 00:41:26,283
Prof. Hiruma!

579
00:41:26,350 --> 00:41:28,052
This was on her desk.

580
00:41:30,588 --> 00:41:31,655
OPERATION CONSENT FORM

581
00:41:31,722 --> 00:41:33,090
KAZUYO MABUCHI

582
00:41:33,157 --> 00:41:34,525
DR. DAIMON IS FREE
TO MAKE ANY DECISION,

583
00:41:34,592 --> 00:41:35,960
INCLUDING THE OPERATION METHOD.

584
00:41:36,093 --> 00:41:37,228
What are you going to do?

585
00:41:45,436 --> 00:41:46,370
Fine.

586
00:41:49,240 --> 00:41:50,941
Prepare the liquid nitrogen.

587
00:42:18,502 --> 00:42:19,737
What are you doing with it?

588
00:42:19,803 --> 00:42:22,573
First, cut a vertical slit on her knee.

589
00:42:22,873 --> 00:42:23,707
Scalpel.

590
00:42:35,953 --> 00:42:36,954
Metzen.

591
00:42:40,624 --> 00:42:41,458
Clamp.

592
00:42:59,376 --> 00:43:02,646
Next, I handle the femur
where the tumor is.

593
00:43:02,846 --> 00:43:04,048
What are you going to do?

594
00:43:06,016 --> 00:43:08,485
Expose the femur.

595
00:43:09,219 --> 00:43:10,054
What?

596
00:43:10,187 --> 00:43:12,389
Start with the collateral ligament.

597
00:43:19,496 --> 00:43:21,765
Dissect the cruciate ligament.
Mosquito.

598
00:43:31,408 --> 00:43:34,545
The femur is exposed.
Bring the liquid nitrogen here.

599
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:37,381
Wait a minute.
Explain what you're doing.

600
00:43:40,017 --> 00:43:43,687
Soak the femur in the nitrogen
at minus 196 degrees Celsius,

601
00:43:43,921 --> 00:43:45,556
and freeze the tumor.

602
00:43:45,756 --> 00:43:48,659
Even if the tumor invaded the bone,
it'll be fine.

603
00:43:48,826 --> 00:43:51,562
Then return it to the original place.

604
00:43:51,629 --> 00:43:53,697
- That's it.
- That's it?

605
00:43:55,065 --> 00:43:57,901
I've never seen
or heard of such an operation.

606
00:43:58,202 --> 00:44:00,704
I'll teach you, so do as I say.

607
00:44:00,771 --> 00:44:03,507
What a reckless operation!

608
00:44:03,707 --> 00:44:05,876
Are you experimenting on Mabuchi?

609
00:44:06,076 --> 00:44:07,277
Please stop her.

610
00:44:07,878 --> 00:44:10,280
Just help me.

611
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:13,250
An operation like this
is a liability issue.

612
00:44:13,951 --> 00:44:17,421
We won't be held
responsible for any of this.

613
00:44:18,255 --> 00:44:20,357
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir.

614
00:44:20,524 --> 00:44:22,226
Hey, where are you going?

615
00:44:22,526 --> 00:44:24,428
I can't do it alone!

616
00:44:24,962 --> 00:44:26,163
Hey!

617
00:44:27,264 --> 00:44:29,266
I can't believe it.

618
00:44:30,768 --> 00:44:33,070
You heard them.

619
00:44:33,437 --> 00:44:36,140
Bring an assistant who will listen.

620
00:44:36,273 --> 00:44:37,474
Enough!

621
00:44:39,410 --> 00:44:41,645
You think someone would help you

622
00:44:42,279 --> 00:44:44,148
with such a reckless operation?

623
00:44:45,849 --> 00:44:46,817
Say it's inoperable.

624
00:44:47,785 --> 00:44:49,153
What are you saying?

625
00:44:49,620 --> 00:44:53,157
With no treatment, Kazuyo Mabuchi
will die in three months.

626
00:44:54,425 --> 00:44:57,027
Better than killing her
with a surgical error.

627
00:44:57,161 --> 00:44:58,595
I will not kill her.

628
00:45:02,032 --> 00:45:04,768
I don't fail.

629
00:45:10,140 --> 00:45:12,776
Hey, help me. Grab that side.

630
00:45:13,343 --> 00:45:15,212
Just the two of us?

631
00:45:15,279 --> 00:45:17,614
We have no choice. Come on, hurry.

632
00:45:19,183 --> 00:45:20,884
Okay.

633
00:45:22,352 --> 00:45:23,187
Here we go.

634
00:45:41,004 --> 00:45:41,972
Dr. Daimon,

635
00:45:42,439 --> 00:45:45,342
we'd like to learn
the new operative method.

636
00:45:45,909 --> 00:45:48,112
- I'm Ayukawa, an intern.
- I'm Tanaka, an intern.

637
00:45:48,245 --> 00:45:51,014
I'm Banharn Phahon Phonphayuhasena.

638
00:45:51,148 --> 00:45:52,616
Forget the greetings.

639
00:45:52,683 --> 00:45:55,219
Turn the bed 10 degrees this way.

640
00:45:55,285 --> 00:45:56,186
Okay.

641
00:46:01,892 --> 00:46:02,826
Ready?

642
00:46:03,627 --> 00:46:05,429
One, two, three.

643
00:46:15,339 --> 00:46:17,641
- Tell me when 20 minutes passes.
- Yes.

644
00:46:24,081 --> 00:46:25,549
Now defrost it at room temperature.

645
00:46:26,316 --> 00:46:28,352
- We'll be using saline solution later.
- Okay.

646
00:46:33,957 --> 00:46:38,529
Perform curettage on the tumor,
and transplant her own bone to it.

647
00:46:38,595 --> 00:46:39,563
Curette.

648
00:46:45,936 --> 00:46:48,372
- Prepare the artificial joint.
- Yes, ma'am.

649
00:47:03,687 --> 00:47:06,723
The amount of bleeding is 450cc.
Vital signs are normal.

650
00:47:07,224 --> 00:47:08,358
Ok, it's done.

651
00:47:21,972 --> 00:47:22,906
Dr. Daimon.

652
00:47:25,442 --> 00:47:28,011
I've learned a lot.
Thank you very much.

653
00:47:28,679 --> 00:47:29,947
Thank you very much.

654
00:47:30,013 --> 00:47:31,148
Thank you very much.

655
00:47:31,648 --> 00:47:32,816
No problem.

656
00:47:33,884 --> 00:47:36,086
You always make me nervous.

657
00:47:36,987 --> 00:47:38,121
Good job.

658
00:47:38,689 --> 00:47:39,756
Good job.

659
00:48:09,519 --> 00:48:13,056
Michiko, I heard
today's operation was tough.

660
00:48:13,123 --> 00:48:15,759
Yeah. I got sore muscles.

661
00:48:15,859 --> 00:48:17,361
Good job.

662
00:48:17,961 --> 00:48:19,563
How was the main branch?

663
00:48:19,830 --> 00:48:22,432
There are so many coward doctors,

664
00:48:22,866 --> 00:48:25,369
but I'll be fine
as long as I can operate.

665
00:48:25,802 --> 00:48:28,438
You do love doing surgeries.

666
00:48:28,605 --> 00:48:30,073
You're a weirdo.

667
00:48:31,141 --> 00:48:33,176
I'll buy you a beer on our way home.

668
00:48:33,377 --> 00:48:35,512
Really? Yay!

669
00:48:35,712 --> 00:48:37,080
Just one though.

670
00:48:37,481 --> 00:48:40,817
I did a ten-million-yen surgery,
and I get one beer?

671
00:48:40,884 --> 00:48:43,020
How stingy! Give me one more.

672
00:48:45,856 --> 00:48:50,260
How smart, having the surgery
at her own hospital!

673
00:48:50,494 --> 00:48:55,499
Usually, lower limb amputation
would have been performed.

674
00:48:55,766 --> 00:48:58,402
Thanks to
the state-of-the-art technique,

675
00:48:59,236 --> 00:49:02,906
her lower limb and life are saved.

676
00:49:04,007 --> 00:49:09,746
The surgeons of Teito Medical Hospital
are very talented.

677
00:49:13,717 --> 00:49:15,252
President,

678
00:49:16,720 --> 00:49:20,624
the chairperson election is approaching.

679
00:49:22,159 --> 00:49:26,330
Bundles of cash will abound once again.

680
00:49:27,998 --> 00:49:32,636
I wonder how many bundles
will fall into my hands this time.

681
00:49:36,073 --> 00:49:39,009
- Excuse me.
- Hi, Tamao.

682
00:49:41,678 --> 00:49:44,748
Professor Hiruma,
let's go to dinner.

683
00:49:46,116 --> 00:49:47,584
Are you hungry after swimming?

684
00:49:49,319 --> 00:49:53,190
Which brand of beef
should we have today?

685
00:49:53,790 --> 00:49:58,462
Kobe? Yonezawa? Miyazaki? Hida?

686
00:49:59,096 --> 00:50:02,399
- I can't decide.
- Yeah.

687
00:50:15,712 --> 00:50:16,713
How is she?

688
00:50:17,214 --> 00:50:19,750
Not much bleeding.
Her vital signs are stable.

689
00:50:21,151 --> 00:50:22,085
I see.

690
00:50:25,122 --> 00:50:29,793
Kondo, regarding today's surgery...

691
00:50:29,860 --> 00:50:32,963
I know. It's confidential.

692
00:50:52,149 --> 00:50:53,016
Professor Mabuchi?

693
00:50:56,153 --> 00:50:57,120
Hey...

694
00:50:59,589 --> 00:51:01,758
What happened...

695
00:51:04,594 --> 00:51:06,096
during my surgery?

696
00:51:13,070 --> 00:51:14,204
I came to collect the bill.

697
00:51:14,337 --> 00:51:17,007
Executive Manager Mabuchi asked me
to hold on to this.

698
00:51:17,741 --> 00:51:19,109
Here's the surgery fee.

699
00:51:19,876 --> 00:51:21,378
Ten million yen. Yes.

700
00:51:27,317 --> 00:51:30,720
Also, do not leak this secret operation...

701
00:51:31,721 --> 00:51:33,924
to the outside world.

702
00:51:34,658 --> 00:51:36,426
I understand.

703
00:51:37,027 --> 00:51:38,028
By the way,

704
00:51:38,261 --> 00:51:42,332
the surgery department is busy
with the chairperson election,

705
00:51:42,732 --> 00:51:44,501
and you need more surgeons.

706
00:51:50,173 --> 00:51:53,977
I believe
Michiko Daimon can be of help.

707
00:51:56,546 --> 00:51:57,414
What a joke!

708
00:51:58,582 --> 00:52:01,218
We can't pay such a ridiculous amount
for every surgery.

709
00:52:02,285 --> 00:52:04,287
Please leave.

710
00:52:07,357 --> 00:52:08,658
More importantly,

711
00:52:09,526 --> 00:52:11,828
the hush money for me to keep quiet

712
00:52:12,829 --> 00:52:16,766
is the same amount as the surgery fee.

713
00:52:20,871 --> 00:52:22,305
Here, it's a melon.

714
00:52:24,441 --> 00:52:25,509
Melon?

715
00:52:26,910 --> 00:52:28,178
Here, it's the bill.

716
00:52:28,245 --> 00:52:30,380
TEN MILLION YEN

717
00:52:32,482 --> 00:52:36,286
I've got ten million yen!

718
00:52:36,553 --> 00:52:39,789
Why didn't you tell me, Kazuyo?

719
00:52:40,757 --> 00:52:44,427
If you had told me,
I, Executive Manager,

720
00:52:44,494 --> 00:52:50,433
would have performed
the perfect operation on you.

721
00:52:52,235 --> 00:52:56,806
Is that so, Prof. Hiruma?

722
00:52:56,873 --> 00:52:59,776
You've been busy holding women,
instead of operative tools.

723
00:53:05,815 --> 00:53:09,119
But I'm glad
that your surgery was a success.

724
00:53:09,186 --> 00:53:11,688
It's thanks to the doctor I found.

725
00:53:11,755 --> 00:53:12,889
On the other hand,

726
00:53:13,823 --> 00:53:17,861
your subordinates ran away
in the middle of the operation.

727
00:53:19,062 --> 00:53:22,165
Wait a minute. Who told you that?

728
00:53:22,299 --> 00:53:24,801
I'll take this case to the committee.

729
00:53:27,437 --> 00:53:29,039
Kazuyo, calm down.

730
00:53:29,639 --> 00:53:30,607
Kazuyo...

731
00:53:31,808 --> 00:53:34,878
Anything but the inquiry commission.

732
00:53:38,181 --> 00:53:41,251
Then would you do me a favor?

733
00:53:41,685 --> 00:53:44,187
Sure. Tell me anything.

734
00:53:44,588 --> 00:53:48,358
I'll do my best.

735
00:53:58,134 --> 00:54:00,437
Well, Executive Manager Hiruma.

736
00:54:01,004 --> 00:54:06,142
Thank you so much for hiring
Michiko Daimon once again.

737
00:54:06,676 --> 00:54:07,744
Hire her?

738
00:54:08,478 --> 00:54:11,715
It must be
some misunderstanding, right?

739
00:54:18,788 --> 00:54:21,858
- Here's the price list.
- Price list?

740
00:54:23,360 --> 00:54:24,227
So expensive!

741
00:54:24,361 --> 00:54:25,595
30,000 YEN PER HOUR

742
00:54:25,695 --> 00:54:29,933
Here are the conditions
you all must follow.

743
00:54:31,935 --> 00:54:32,769
Please take one.

744
00:54:40,076 --> 00:54:41,144
What the heck is this?

745
00:54:41,378 --> 00:54:43,346
These are her working conditions.

746
00:54:43,713 --> 00:54:46,983
"Support a prof's thesis,
including research."

747
00:54:47,117 --> 00:54:48,218
I won't do that.

748
00:54:48,351 --> 00:54:50,854
- "Accompany doctors to conferences?"
- I won't do that.

749
00:54:51,121 --> 00:54:53,456
- "Drive to and from golf course."
- I won't do that.

750
00:54:53,823 --> 00:54:56,660
- "Cover up your lovers."
- I won't do that.

751
00:54:56,793 --> 00:54:59,062
- "Go out for drinks."
- I won't do that.

752
00:54:59,195 --> 00:55:02,132
- "Make the professors' rounds."
- As you see,

753
00:55:02,999 --> 00:55:06,636
I won't do any of the things
that don't require a medical license.

754
00:55:10,006 --> 00:55:14,511
You're going to hire a person like her?

755
00:55:16,146 --> 00:55:18,081
You know, Daimon,

756
00:55:19,916 --> 00:55:24,020
you're wearing
such flashy clothes again.

757
00:55:24,154 --> 00:55:28,291
Akira, add one more condition.

758
00:55:28,358 --> 00:55:29,192
Sure.

759
00:55:36,066 --> 00:55:39,235
No claims that are irrelevant
to a medical license.

760
00:55:42,172 --> 00:55:44,507
I will wear what I want to wear.

761
00:55:46,009 --> 00:55:47,077
That's it.

762
00:55:49,679 --> 00:55:50,947
"That's it?"

763
00:55:51,014 --> 00:55:52,949
- "That's it?"
- Don't make fun of us!

764
00:55:53,717 --> 00:55:54,918
VISITOR PASS

765
00:56:09,499 --> 00:56:13,169
Already starting a therapy?
You seem to be doing well.

766
00:56:14,738 --> 00:56:17,841
When did you find out
that I was the patient?

767
00:56:19,242 --> 00:56:21,144
Did you know before the surgery?

768
00:56:22,979 --> 00:56:24,047
Yes, I did.

769
00:56:24,948 --> 00:56:26,216
How did you find out?

770
00:56:29,185 --> 00:56:30,553
The height of your heels.

771
00:56:31,221 --> 00:56:34,624
While the right heel was 10cm,
the left was shorter by 2cm.

772
00:56:35,492 --> 00:56:40,930
Didn't you have difficulty walking
due to the tumor in your femur?

773
00:56:44,401 --> 00:56:47,771
Now you can wear
10cm heels on both feet.

774
00:56:48,438 --> 00:56:50,740
- Take care.
- Is that all?

775
00:56:51,975 --> 00:56:53,543
Something else to say to me?

776
00:56:56,679 --> 00:56:58,715
A freelancer like you

777
00:56:59,482 --> 00:57:03,953
was able to get a job
at this top-level university hospital.

778
00:57:04,354 --> 00:57:05,722
Don't forget who to thank.

779
00:57:07,524 --> 00:57:10,093
I don't like obligations like that.

780
00:57:11,027 --> 00:57:12,862
Don't get full of yourself.

781
00:57:13,930 --> 00:57:16,833
You're just one of my race horses.

782
00:57:23,473 --> 00:57:24,974
Now that you're here,

783
00:57:25,809 --> 00:57:28,745
you must run desperately for me.

784
00:57:30,513 --> 00:57:34,083
I can do that
without a medical license.

785
00:57:34,150 --> 00:57:35,385
So what?

786
00:57:38,121 --> 00:57:41,658
If you go against me,
I'll put you down.

787
00:57:55,338 --> 00:57:58,041
I should've said it was inoperable.

788
00:58:00,543 --> 00:58:02,145
I heard that.

789
00:58:03,713 --> 00:58:05,582
Women are scary.

790
00:58:07,450 --> 00:58:08,685
Michiko Daimon,

791
00:58:10,286 --> 00:58:12,655
welcome to my surgery department.

792
00:58:17,160 --> 00:58:18,127
I won't do that.

793
00:58:19,696 --> 00:58:24,567
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

794
00:58:29,072 --> 00:58:30,440
She's troublesome.

795
00:58:32,175 --> 00:58:37,113
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

796
00:58:45,688 --> 00:58:47,156
Let's start.

797
00:58:48,791 --> 00:58:49,626
Scalpel.

798
00:58:51,594 --> 00:58:53,563
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

799
00:58:54,063 --> 00:58:56,866
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

800
01:00:06,703 --> 01:00:08,871
THE STORY DEPICTED
IN THIS DRAMA IS FICTITIOUS.

801
01:00:09,005 --> 01:00:10,940
It's a relapse!

802
01:00:11,074 --> 01:00:14,243
Is it not good to
know if it's a relapse or not?

803
01:00:14,377 --> 01:00:16,546
Hiruma's reputation will crumble.

804
01:00:16,679 --> 01:00:19,782
I will decide
if the operation is performed.

805
01:00:19,882 --> 01:00:22,218
- Remove all the peritoneum?
- You'll get sued.

806
01:00:22,285 --> 01:00:23,620
I'm fired?
